WEBVTT

00:01.860 --> 00:03.730
An elite boy's school.

00:03.900 --> 00:06.870
I transferred after the semester began.

00:06.970 --> 00:09.670
I had no idea what was waiting for me.

00:09.970 --> 00:12.570
I thought it was just a school full of guys...

00:12.810 --> 00:14.110
...but why do I see a girl?

00:14.240 --> 00:15.340
I'm a guy!

00:15.440 --> 00:15.970
Huh?

00:16.080 --> 00:17.310
But that skirt...

00:17.410 --> 00:19.380
What are you saying?
You're going to wear it too.

00:19.480 --> 00:19.950
What?

00:20.050 --> 00:22.240
The three of us are in this together.

00:22.420 --> 00:24.080
Let's do a great job, okay?

00:24.190 --> 00:25.680
No!

00:25.950 --> 00:29.480
And this is how my life as a princess began...

00:30.290 --> 00:36.930
<i>After I met you, you shed</i> <i>some light onto my heart.</i>

00:37.070 --> 00:43.670
<i>I spent my days doing the</i> <i>same things all the time.</i>

00:44.570 --> 00:49.640
<i>I know what I want to</i> <i>say to you every time.</i>

00:49.780 --> 00:56.340
<i>I always have them</i> <i>hidden inside my heart.</i>

00:57.320 --> 01:02.020
<i>I know it's an important feeling...</i>

01:02.260 --> 01:07.700
<i>...and I'm keeping it warm</i> <i>to give it to you someday.</i>

01:10.000 --> 01:15.670
<i>Sound of the bells</i>
<i>I hear from far away.</i>

01:15.770 --> 01:22.580
<i>...makes my heart beat faster and</i> <i>cuts through the sky like the wind.</i>

01:22.710 --> 01:29.380
<i>After I met you, you shed</i> <i>some light onto my heart.</i>

01:29.480 --> 01:35.190
<i>I spent my days doing the</i> <i>same things all the time.</i>

01:35.390 --> 01:42.060
<i>And when it's time to tell you</i> <i>the things I've been wanting to say...</i>

01:42.200 --> 01:47.860
<i>You're my sunshine, an eternal smile!</i>

01:48.170 --> 01:58.170
<i>Our prologue, to this exciting story...</i>

02:00.320 --> 02:05.950
<i>Chorus Concert of Sweat and Tears.</i>

02:06.390 --> 02:10.260
<i>2nd semester</i>

02:14.630 --> 02:16.120
So you stayed up all night?

02:16.400 --> 02:18.390
I didn't finish my homework so...

02:19.130 --> 02:21.000
I said you can copy my work, right?

02:21.570 --> 02:24.540
But I won't learn anything that way...

02:24.970 --> 02:27.500
You're really stubborn when it comes to things like that.

02:27.610 --> 02:29.130
Can't you adapt to changing circumstances?

02:29.340 --> 02:30.240
Leave me alone!

02:30.350 --> 02:33.180
Now now, that's the good thing about Mikoto.

02:34.720 --> 02:36.650
We had fun this summer, right?

02:36.750 --> 02:38.220
Fun?

02:38.350 --> 02:41.220
We stayed in the dorms most of the time,
I don't think it was a memorable summer.

02:41.320 --> 02:43.590
But it was much better than going home...

02:45.790 --> 02:48.790
I mean it was fun to visit Akira's home.

02:49.200 --> 02:51.130
Why are you calling him Akira now?

02:51.230 --> 02:55.190
Lots of things happened, and we became very close friends.

02:55.600 --> 02:59.010
Yeah, something really big happened.

02:59.310 --> 03:01.900
What exactly happened?

03:05.550 --> 03:07.280
Seeya, Mikoto.

03:07.480 --> 03:09.750
I hope you don't collapse due to lack of sleep.

03:09.950 --> 03:11.250
Wait a minute, Kouno!

03:17.390 --> 03:19.860
I wonder if Mikoto is okay.

03:20.100 --> 03:22.430
They might surround him before he falls down.

03:22.560 --> 03:25.060
He's much more careless than usual.

03:27.270 --> 03:30.270
Let go of me!

03:27.470 --> 03:30.270
<i>Princess Mikoto! How I longed for you!</i>

03:30.370 --> 03:31.700
It's been a while!

03:32.870 --> 03:34.270
See?

03:37.180 --> 03:38.240
Good morning.

03:38.550 --> 03:40.070
Good morning, Akira.

03:40.450 --> 03:42.150
What's wrong, Akira?

03:42.250 --> 03:45.650
You're not going to call us by our first name, Akira?

03:46.460 --> 03:48.190
Umm...

03:50.730 --> 03:53.420
Good morning, Tohru, Yujirou.

03:53.900 --> 03:56.390
He's a tough customer, unlike Mikoto.

03:56.500 --> 04:00.960
If we pick on Mikoto like this, he'll snap and get all angry.

04:01.070 --> 04:04.370
But he just deals with it smoothly. Good job, Akira.

04:04.470 --> 04:06.810
What are you saying?
Are you making fun of me?

04:06.940 --> 04:09.280
We didn't mean any harm.

04:09.510 --> 04:10.950
Princess!

04:11.750 --> 04:14.270
You're beautiful, just as I remembered!

04:14.380 --> 04:17.720
In the sanctuary of our hearts we haven't forgotten about you.

04:17.850 --> 04:19.190
What are they saying?

04:19.290 --> 04:24.060
I'm guessing they were trying to get girlfriends during the summer...

04:24.230 --> 04:26.020
...but their plan failed.

04:26.160 --> 04:27.560
Losers, eh?

04:27.660 --> 04:30.660
So they're seeking spiritual support.

04:30.970 --> 04:32.090
Princesses!

04:32.200 --> 04:33.430
Show us mercy!

04:33.540 --> 04:35.270
Provide us with the warmth of your hearts!

04:35.640 --> 04:37.870
Please!

04:38.410 --> 04:41.310
Tohru, it's our first job of the new semester.

04:41.410 --> 04:42.140
Yeah.

04:52.350 --> 04:53.290
Princess!

04:53.390 --> 04:54.620
This is great!

04:54.760 --> 04:55.950
The best!

04:56.490 --> 04:58.260
They're professionals...

05:03.000 --> 05:05.060
This is it for today, right?

05:05.270 --> 05:07.500
Yeah, but...

05:09.400 --> 05:11.340
This is an announcement from the student organization.

05:11.440 --> 05:15.540
Princesses, please come to the student organization room immediately.

05:15.640 --> 05:18.840
I repeat, this is an announcement from the student organization.

05:18.980 --> 05:22.280
Princesses, please come to the student organization room immediately.

05:22.420 --> 05:23.750
I knew it.

05:23.850 --> 05:26.750
<i>Student organization room</i>

05:27.690 --> 05:28.680
Now...

05:29.220 --> 05:31.780
The reason why I had you guys come here today...

05:31.930 --> 05:35.130
is to discuss your schedules for this semester.

05:35.900 --> 05:36.860
<i>Here.</i>

05:36.230 --> 05:36.860
This is it.

05:37.330 --> 05:38.300
Please.

05:38.870 --> 05:42.860
Your jobs are going to be a little difficult this semester.

05:45.370 --> 05:49.240
Leaving aside the fact that you still have to do cheering and other jobs...

05:49.380 --> 05:51.310
...as you can see from the plan...

05:51.410 --> 05:54.380
...we have lots of huge events bunched up together.

05:54.580 --> 05:57.080
The sports festival, chorus concert, school festival...

05:57.220 --> 05:59.480
...elections for the student organization and much more.

05:59.690 --> 06:02.350
I guess our first order of business is the chorus concert.

06:02.490 --> 06:03.750
Chorus concert?

06:03.860 --> 06:05.660
What are we supposed to do?

06:06.030 --> 06:09.160
If I had to say it in a simple way, then it's the "curtain raiser."

06:09.330 --> 06:10.090
Curtain raiser?

06:10.200 --> 06:11.000
That's right.

06:11.100 --> 06:13.930
Do you think a chorus concert with bunch of guys singing in rough voices...

06:14.040 --> 06:15.630
...will be exciting?

06:15.800 --> 06:17.240
It's not, right?

06:18.040 --> 06:20.200
So before the concert begins, the princesses...

06:20.310 --> 06:23.570
...are going to sing and dance on stage to get things started.

06:23.950 --> 06:25.000
Sing?

06:25.280 --> 06:26.440
Dance?

06:28.920 --> 06:32.250
You can choose the songs and choreograph the dance any way you like.

06:32.390 --> 06:34.910
But make it something that will excite the crowd.

06:35.590 --> 06:39.320
And if you can't think of anything, then we'll make something for you.

06:39.490 --> 06:42.260
The songs and MC intros will last about 10 minutes.

06:42.400 --> 06:44.730
Good luck with your performance on stage!

06:44.870 --> 06:46.770
Are we...

06:45.630 --> 06:47.170
<i>...upcoming idols or something?</i>

06:47.270 --> 06:48.570
Stop complaining.

06:48.670 --> 06:51.110
This is one of the jobs of a princess.

06:51.270 --> 06:52.400
That's right.

06:52.840 --> 06:55.740
Then you did this too, right, president?

06:55.880 --> 06:57.610
By the way, what did you sing?

06:57.750 --> 06:58.710
Me?

06:58.810 --> 07:01.870
Back in my days, I had to wear a kimono.

07:02.750 --> 07:04.810
I sang Japanese enka with all my heart.

07:17.830 --> 07:18.800
Enka...

07:18.930 --> 07:20.930
He sure got us with that one...

07:21.070 --> 07:23.660
He's always one step ahead of us.

07:23.810 --> 07:26.040
It's not fair...

07:26.810 --> 07:30.970
Mikoto, you've been rather quiet, but how come you're not resisting?

07:31.510 --> 07:32.480
Mikoto?

07:32.880 --> 07:34.650
What's wrong? Mikoto!

07:34.750 --> 07:35.410
Mikoto!

07:37.090 --> 07:39.110
I just don't want to sing.

07:39.350 --> 07:40.120
What?

07:41.890 --> 07:45.550
Well, you're always saying "No!" or "I don't want to do it!"

07:45.660 --> 07:46.590
That's right!

07:46.700 --> 07:49.490
This is different! I just can't do singing!

07:49.930 --> 07:50.630
Why?

07:55.140 --> 07:56.570
Because I...

07:57.610 --> 07:58.700
I...

08:00.310 --> 08:05.770
I'm tone-deaf!

08:05.880 --> 08:10.750
<i>Karaoke</i>

08:11.050 --> 08:14.250
So basically, Mikoto can't sing at all.

08:15.190 --> 08:18.250
Anyway, let's just find out how bad he is.

08:18.390 --> 08:19.090
Yeah.

08:19.190 --> 08:22.820
We can't choose a song if we don't know how bad you are.

08:23.160 --> 08:25.960
Stop stressing that I'm bad!

08:26.070 --> 08:32.100
You're just a burden, stop complaining and start singing.

08:32.470 --> 08:33.100
What?

08:34.410 --> 08:38.310
Wait a minute, why did you choose a song on your own?

08:38.450 --> 08:40.640
We came here to find out how bad Mikoto is, right?

08:41.120 --> 08:43.920
Don't worry about it, since we came here, we might as well sing.

08:44.120 --> 08:47.780
Arisada is good with enka, but he's also good at ballad songs too.

08:47.920 --> 08:50.590
He's so much better than some of the singers out there.

08:50.760 --> 08:52.730
You guys won't regret it.

08:55.830 --> 08:58.230
This is...

08:57.030 --> 08:58.230
<i>bad...</i>

08:58.930 --> 09:01.660
We're moving to a different room.

09:10.650 --> 09:15.850
Maybe they just came here to have fun from the very beginning...

09:18.250 --> 09:21.220
Now that we've settled down...
Shall we begin?

09:21.360 --> 09:24.220
Mikoto, is there anything you can sing?

09:28.830 --> 09:29.420
No.

09:29.630 --> 09:32.660
We didn't come all the way here to hear you say no!

09:33.000 --> 09:36.700
I guess we'll pick some songs randomly and make him sing.

09:41.840 --> 09:42.870
How about this?

09:43.010 --> 09:46.680
We hear this song a lot these days, the melody is rather simple, too.

09:46.820 --> 09:47.540
Here.

09:48.780 --> 09:51.180
<i>I want to give you my smile</i>

10:06.000 --> 10:10.100
<i>Karaoke</i>

10:10.470 --> 10:11.870
That felt so good.

10:11.970 --> 10:13.240
You did good, Arisada.

10:13.370 --> 10:16.780
It was nice to hear your beautiful singing voice after such a long time.

10:16.980 --> 10:18.950
I'm very satisfied.

10:21.880 --> 10:23.220
How did it go?

10:23.650 --> 10:24.980
Horrible.

10:25.250 --> 10:27.150
He needs some serious training.

10:27.320 --> 10:28.190
What?

10:39.270 --> 10:41.100
Well, good luck!

10:42.170 --> 10:43.800
Should we go play billiards?

10:43.940 --> 10:46.500
I want to see Arisada hit that cue ball with finesse.

10:46.610 --> 10:49.440
I'll feel embarrassed if you say things like that.

10:49.540 --> 10:51.810
I guess they just wanted to have some fun.

10:51.910 --> 10:53.180
You're right.

10:58.420 --> 11:03.150
But how do we make Mikoto sing better?

11:01.060 --> 11:03.150
<i>Shihoudani</i>

11:04.130 --> 11:06.820
I guess he's going to have to practice steadily.

11:06.960 --> 11:10.230
We only have 2 weeks until the chorus concert.

11:13.270 --> 11:14.460
Tohru!

11:14.570 --> 11:15.330
Yes?

11:15.840 --> 11:19.540
There was a call for you earlier, it was from your younger sister.

11:22.310 --> 11:24.540
I understand, thank you.

11:42.760 --> 11:45.560
Aren't you going to call her back?

11:46.630 --> 11:47.690
Yeah...

12:20.340 --> 12:23.330
They're practicing for the concert.

12:23.440 --> 12:23.910
Yeah...

12:24.310 --> 12:25.830
You guys!

12:25.970 --> 12:27.840
I was looking for you!

12:28.210 --> 12:29.770
Natasho!

12:29.880 --> 12:32.440
Did you guys decide what song to sing?

12:32.550 --> 12:33.570
No, not yet.

12:33.680 --> 12:35.980
I want you guys to decide as soon as possible!

12:36.080 --> 12:38.640
I don't know what kind of wardrobe I should make!

12:38.750 --> 12:42.520
Well, you're going to make our wardrobes anyway...

12:42.660 --> 12:44.960
...so you can just make whatever you want.

12:45.060 --> 12:45.990
That's right.

12:46.090 --> 12:48.460
Even if it doesn't match the song, we'll match it up with the choreography.

12:48.860 --> 12:50.390
What? Really?

12:50.700 --> 12:53.860
Actually, I was secretly making this wardrobe.

12:53.970 --> 12:57.840
It will be based on a girl's uniform, the top will look like a bolero.

12:57.940 --> 13:02.100
I want to make a tight skirt, but it won't have much volume on stage...

13:02.210 --> 13:04.110
...so it has to be fluffy...

13:04.350 --> 13:06.410
You can do whatever you like.

13:06.510 --> 13:07.570
We don't mind.

13:07.680 --> 13:09.080
Then I'll bring them later!

13:12.190 --> 13:15.450
What? How to sing better?

13:15.820 --> 13:18.220
Yeah. You got any good ideas?

13:22.230 --> 13:23.390
Got it!

13:25.900 --> 13:29.170
Why do I have to put that on my head to sing?

13:29.270 --> 13:32.970
I don't know how it works theoretically, but Akira said he saw it on TV.

13:33.470 --> 13:35.470
You have no right to refuse.

13:35.610 --> 13:36.910
Just wear it!

13:45.990 --> 13:48.910
You!

13:46.920 --> 13:48.910
<i>Okay, okay, I'm sorry!</i>

13:49.020 --> 13:50.320
We won't laugh.

13:50.460 --> 13:53.450
Thanks for waiting!
I have your wardrobes!

13:55.060 --> 13:56.460
Try them on!

13:56.600 --> 13:57.720
O-Okay...

14:00.970 --> 14:02.830
Mikoto, we'll practice with the outfits on.

14:03.200 --> 14:05.110
What? You're leaving?

14:05.910 --> 14:09.400
We want to practice where there's privacy.

14:09.580 --> 14:12.310
You'll just have to wait until the show.

14:15.450 --> 14:17.540
No!

14:33.970 --> 14:37.530
This just isn't working for me...

14:38.310 --> 14:39.710
I'll just lip-sync.

14:39.810 --> 14:40.870
Mikoto...

14:41.540 --> 14:44.480
You guys do it yourselves then!

14:44.580 --> 14:46.340
He's acting like a spoiled kid again.

14:46.450 --> 14:47.240
But...

14:47.550 --> 14:48.450
Tohru...

14:57.930 --> 14:58.950
Sayaka...

15:13.310 --> 15:14.780
Why did you come here?

15:15.610 --> 15:17.100
Tohru...

15:20.780 --> 15:23.580
Why are you dressed like that?

15:25.150 --> 15:26.750
I totally forgot!

15:26.890 --> 15:29.480
I have the princess wardrobe on!

15:31.530 --> 15:32.790
Well...

15:33.190 --> 15:36.390
We were just practicing for an amateur performance contest.

15:36.530 --> 15:38.830
It's one of the school events.

15:38.970 --> 15:40.130
Really?

15:40.370 --> 15:41.700
That's right.

15:41.800 --> 15:43.800
Who is she?

15:44.010 --> 15:49.540
She's the daughter of the people who took care of me.

15:50.810 --> 15:52.750
I see...

15:53.610 --> 15:57.450
Sayaka, they told you not to come here, right?

15:57.620 --> 16:01.650
I know, but you didn't come back home for the summer...

16:01.790 --> 16:04.090
...and you never answered your phone!

16:04.230 --> 16:07.090
You came here without telling your folks?

16:07.600 --> 16:09.860
I told them not to tell you where this school is located...

16:10.060 --> 16:12.060
It's all your fault, Tohru!

16:12.470 --> 16:14.030
Come back home!

16:14.140 --> 16:17.070
I can't live my life without you, Tohru!

16:21.680 --> 16:25.510
I can only think of you as my younger sister.

16:26.650 --> 16:29.670
Can you think of me as your older brother?

16:29.820 --> 16:31.310
Otherwise, I can't go back.

16:31.450 --> 16:32.390
No!

16:32.550 --> 16:36.890
I've always dreamt of becoming your wife someday.

16:37.120 --> 16:40.720
I was really happy when I found out we weren't related by blood.

16:41.500 --> 16:45.660
I thought you felt the same way about me, that you would always love me.

16:46.000 --> 16:50.840
And if we get married, we can be a real family along with my parents.

16:50.970 --> 16:55.030
An orphan like you should be real happy with that.

16:55.280 --> 16:57.440
Anyway, I'm contacting your father.

16:57.580 --> 16:59.910
No! I'm not going back until you promise to come back!

17:00.080 --> 17:01.450
You know!

17:01.950 --> 17:02.940
Yujirou.

17:03.180 --> 17:06.180
There's no point in attacking your big brother.

17:06.450 --> 17:09.290
Who are you? What are you saying?

17:09.420 --> 17:10.520
Yujirou?

17:11.090 --> 17:15.330
This was supposed to be a secret, but your brother is not interested in girls.

17:15.530 --> 17:16.160
What?

17:19.800 --> 17:21.200
That's not true!

17:21.300 --> 17:24.200
He was involved with some girl before!

17:24.310 --> 17:28.000
It doesn't matter what you say, he's dating me now.

17:28.310 --> 17:30.640
You think you can fool me like that?

17:30.910 --> 17:33.610
I'm serious.

17:34.650 --> 17:36.950
You want some proof?

18:09.780 --> 18:12.950
Well? You still don't believe me?

18:14.160 --> 18:16.590
Then let's keep going...

18:20.360 --> 18:21.920
No, it can't be!

18:22.100 --> 18:24.790
It can't be...

18:26.130 --> 18:29.370
No!

18:30.470 --> 18:32.440
Yujirou, you...

18:32.610 --> 18:33.670
What?

18:33.910 --> 18:36.900
You should be happy since she went back home.

18:37.010 --> 18:38.950
But you know...

18:39.050 --> 18:40.780
Hey, where's Mikoto?

18:42.520 --> 18:44.880
So you guys are like that now, huh?

18:45.090 --> 18:46.520
Don't take it seriously!

18:46.690 --> 18:49.750
That was just to ward her off.

18:50.090 --> 18:55.220
She was just surprised to see us kiss, she might be back after she calms down.

18:55.430 --> 18:59.490
You better have something to say when she does.

18:59.600 --> 19:00.860
Next time...

19:01.000 --> 19:04.770
Maybe we have to do more than kiss.

19:04.870 --> 19:06.170
What do you think?

19:06.270 --> 19:08.000
Yujirou...

19:12.410 --> 19:15.380
Looks like Kouno's got his hands full.

19:15.980 --> 19:17.470
Looks like it.

19:17.650 --> 19:22.680
Maybe he feels better when he's doing the princess job.

19:22.890 --> 19:24.190
Maybe.

19:24.330 --> 19:29.860
This princess job is helping Tohru both financially and psychologically.

19:30.160 --> 19:34.800
You may be tone-deaf, but that's nothing compared to what he goes through.

19:34.970 --> 19:36.900
Yeah, you're right.

19:37.040 --> 19:39.700
Tone-deaf is nothing.

19:38.210 --> 19:39.700
<i>Stop saying that!</i>

19:41.440 --> 19:45.070
I have to deal with
Sayaka sooner or later.

19:45.580 --> 19:47.910
But for now...

19:57.320 --> 20:00.590
And now, we'll begin the chorus concert.

20:00.730 --> 20:03.960
Before we do, here are the flowers that bloom within our school.

20:04.100 --> 20:08.260
Please enjoy the opening ceremony by our princesses!

20:20.950 --> 20:23.710
<i>She's the sort of girl</i> <i>who's always in fashion...</i>

20:23.980 --> 20:26.750
<i>And she has the cutest</i> <i>behind that we know of.</i>

20:27.020 --> 20:29.890
<i>Please look my way, Honey!</i>

20:30.160 --> 20:35.460
<i>Well it's just that...</i>
<i>Just, just because...</i>

20:35.560 --> 20:41.300
<i>Oh please, oh please...</i>
<i>Please don't break my heart.</i>

20:41.470 --> 20:47.770
<i>My heart aches real bad.</i>

20:48.080 --> 20:52.240
<i>No, no, no!</i>
<i>Don't stare at me like that!</i>

20:53.010 --> 20:55.850
<i>Honey Flash!</i>

20:56.480 --> 20:58.390
<i>I'm going to change!</i>

21:13.570 --> 21:14.590
Mikoto!

21:14.740 --> 21:16.670
What was that sullen look on your face?

21:16.770 --> 21:18.430
You said your lines unwillingly!

21:18.570 --> 21:21.130
But it's really embarrassing!

21:21.380 --> 21:23.000
I did it right, didn't I?

21:23.180 --> 21:25.510
That's not what we're talking about!

21:31.420 --> 21:34.620
Well, I guess it's okay since they were entertained.

21:41.760 --> 21:49.330
<i>If you're sad and feeling</i> <i>down, then call out to me.</i>

21:49.440 --> 21:57.500
<i>I'll be in the area, so let</i> <i>me know what's bothering you.</i>

21:58.010 --> 22:05.350
<i>If you're all by yourself,</i> <i>then you'll forget how to smile.</i>

22:05.450 --> 22:13.190
<i>A smile is something you</i> <i>share with another person.</i>

22:13.330 --> 22:23.330
<i>Hey, the future you can see</i> <i>from the classroom window...</i>

22:23.570 --> 22:30.170
<i>...is getting larger after</i> <i>taking in the sunlight.</i>

22:30.510 --> 22:32.000
<i>Smile at me!</i>

22:32.150 --> 22:39.880
<i>A smile is what makes you feel energetic!</i>

22:39.990 --> 22:45.980
<i>I want to give some smiles to you...</i>

22:46.130 --> 22:48.150
<i>...right away.</i>

22:48.430 --> 22:58.430
<i>In order for you to lift</i> <i>your head up and start walking.</i>

23:04.980 --> 23:09.940
Next Episode, The Princesses'
Existence in Danger
